## Scientific lifecycle

Development, pilot, and locked data use different scenario variants and
campaign IDs. Pilot outcomes may tune prompts, thresholds, feasibility rules,
and `r`; locked outcomes may not. Any substantive post-freeze change requires a
new campaign version and fresh affected entries.

Create a pilot schedule from explicit cells:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.freeze_protocol \
  --campaign-id pilot-v1 \
  --mode pilot \
  --cells /path/to/pilot_cells.json \
  --seed 20260811
```

Inspect and reserve the next sequential attempt:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign experiments/runs/pilot-v1 status
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign experiments/runs/pilot-v1 next
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign experiments/runs/pilot-v1 begin
```

`begin` reserves a new attempt identity but does not manufacture evidence. The
episode driver must immediately create an `AttemptRecorder` at that exact
schedule/attempt path, start video before scene reset, and seal the registry
once. A valid system failure is sealed and retained; it is never retried.

After an independently evidenced infrastructure interruption, retry remains
blocked until a recovery JSON report and distinct raw records prove service
restoration, two consecutive successful health checks, and a later
non-mutating smoke test. Bind that report exactly once with:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign \
  experiments/runs/<campaign_id> authorize-retry \
  <schedule_id> environment/recovery/<report>.json
```

The engines in `harness/engines.py` are instrumentation pilots, explicitly
marked invalid for publication and refused for locked campaigns. Run one
controlled path (or add `--all`) with:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign \
  experiments/runs/pilot-v1 execute --engine scripted-pass
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign \
  experiments/runs/pilot-v1 execute --engine scripted-failure
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign \
  experiments/runs/pilot-v1 execute --engine mujoco-pass
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign \
  experiments/runs/pilot-v1 execute --engine mujoco-failure
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_campaign \
  experiments/runs/pilot-v1 execute --engine service-live
```

The MuJoCo engines validate reset/render/record/oracle plumbing using a declared
direct scene action; they do not establish robot-trajectory performance.
`service-live` exercises one real loopback model transport and its
infrastructure/system-failure classification; it is also pilot-only.

The separate `ProductionMujocoEngine` is marked publication-valid and invokes
the current role/runtime/MuJoCo stack, but it is intentionally fail-closed to
exactly profile `T5`, executor `mujoco`, and scenario `NM02`. It rejects merged
topologies, every ablation/baseline, and the other 61 scenario templates rather
than simulating them. The runner exposes this path as `--engine
production-mujoco` for pilots and an exactly approved locked campaign. Locked
configuration, video settings, setup metadata, engine identity, and live source
are rebound to the manifest; manual locked `begin`, `seal`, and `reconcile`
transitions are refused. This command is valid only for supported T5/NM02 cells.
Consequently, it still cannot execute or resume the full locked matrix.

Visual provenance is request-scoped. Every visual model call must contain one
and only one distinct registered capture, and its model-call start binds exactly
one `frame_request_id`. Nested calls may each use different captures, and
sequential Validator calls may accumulate different views, but one request
containing multiple distinct images is intentionally rejected as ambiguous.
This singular contract is a current implementation limitation, not permission
to weaken the design's multi-view validation requirement.

After pilots pass and the powered repetition count is fixed, freeze a locked
campaign. Freezing does **not** authorize execution:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.freeze_protocol \
  --campaign-id locked-v1 \
  --mode locked \
  --repetitions <pilot-powered-r> \
  --seed <frozen-master-seed> \
  --metadata /path/to/final_locked_metadata.json
```

Locked metadata must include the exact `execution_engine` identity:
`engine_id`, dotted `module`, `class_name`, repository-relative `source_path`,
and `source_sha256`. The source must be covered by provenance. The manifest
also freezes the outcome/reference and exact matrix/profile contrast families
derived from the schedule; analysis-time alternatives are post-hoc. The draft
preregistration, unresolved model IDs/hashes, and unfrozen power decision remain
hard blockers.

Locked `begin` calls fail until the user sends exactly:

```text
APPROVE LOCKED CAMPAIGN <campaign_id> <protocol_sha256>
```

Whitespace changes, extra prose, a different campaign ID, or a different hash
are rejected. Pilot campaigns need no locked approval. Human-participant work
is not authorized by this approval: it additionally requires documented ethics
approval, consent/withdrawal, privacy, retention, recruitment, and compensation
procedures. Real-robot work is also outside the default campaign and requires a
separate safety screen and explicit authorization. Unsafe ablations remain
synthetic/MuJoCo-only.

Regenerate analysis and audit artifacts with:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.analyze experiments/runs/<campaign_id>
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.audit_campaign \
  experiments/runs/<campaign_id> --write-checksums --check-live-source
```

The binary confirmatory fit and its power analysis use explicit immutable JSON
rows/config inputs and refuse to overwrite outputs:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.harness.mixed_effects fit \
  --rows /path/to/excluded_pilot_rows.json \
  --config /path/to/frozen_fit_config.json \
  --output /path/to/fit.json
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.harness.mixed_effects power \
  --rows /path/to/excluded_pilot_rows.json \
  --config /path/to/frozen_power_config.json \
  --output /path/to/power.json
```

Each command writes a source/input/config-bound result and adjacent SHA-256
file. A command that returns `estimable=false` is a documented analysis
failure, not permission to fall back to an ordinary logistic model.

`--write-checksums` is one-time finalization. An existing manifest is verified,
never regenerated over a mismatch. The final `audit.json` is also immutable and
bound by `audit.sha256`; use `--stdout-only` for later diagnostics.

An incomplete campaign may be inspected with `--allow-incomplete`; that flag
does not make it complete. Analysis reports unresolved assigned episodes as
`NOT ESTIMABLE` with bounds rather than silently dropping them.

## Tests

The experiment tests are standard-library `unittest` tests and do not require
pytest:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_experiment_*.py'
```

Tests validate contracts; they are not a substitute for profile preflights,
successful and controlled-failure pilots, or artifact review.
After the v6 source-starvation and v7 raw-cadence diagnoses, the final
consolidated experiment suite passes 190/190. Focused checks also pass for the atomic task/overview
pair, request/frame/redaction linkage, continuous evidence pump, CFR collision
filter, realtime rebasing, and MuJoCo-time controller speed/settling path. A
fresh production pilot remains required; these tests must not be described as
a successful behavioral run.

Run the calibration entry points separately; each output remains calibration
evidence rather than an experimental result:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.run_invariants
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.build_components
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.preflight_profiles
.venv/bin/python -m experiments.preflight_scenarios
```

## Scale and resource estimate

The default fresh-reference schedule contains:

```text
main comparison        248r episodes
topology comparison    120r episodes
mechanism ablations    128r episodes
model sensitivity      1,200 episodes
total                   496r + 1,200 episodes
```

Thus the design range is 6,160 episodes at `r=10`, 8,640 at `r=15`, 11,120 at
`r=20`, and 13,600 at `r=25`. This intentionally does not reuse T5 results
across matrices after outcomes are known. The worst-case preservation envelope
is three times those attempt counts if every entry suffers the maximum allowed
infrastructure interruptions; it is not an expected run count.

Sequential wall time is `episodes × pilot mean attempt duration`. For planning,
at 3/5/10 minutes per episode, `r=10` is about 308/513/1,027 hours and `r=25`
is about 680/1,133/2,267 hours. Inference calls are
`episodes × pilot mean calls per episode` plus declared preflight calls. A fixed
call count cannot honestly be quoted before pilots because receding-horizon
cycles, monitoring polls, repairs, and timeouts vary by observed behavior.

Video capacity is similarly empirical. At five minutes per episode, a combined
composite-plus-robot-camera bitrate of 6/12/20 Mbit/s produces roughly
225/450/750 MB per attempt. At `r=10`, video alone is then approximately
1.39/2.77/4.62 TB; at `r=25`, approximately 3.06/6.12/10.2 TB. Add exact request
frames, raw model calls, JSONL logs, retry attempts, and at least a 25% safety
margin. The freeze report must replace these sensitivities with pilot-measured
duration, bitrate, inference-call, and artifact-size distributions, and must
record a fresh `df -h` capacity check before asking for locked approval.

The latest documented capacity check, at `2026-08-11T06:28:14Z`, found
1,650,659,434,496 bytes available (1.650659 TB / 1.501266 TiB). Reserving 20%
or 25% of that free space leaves only 1.320528 TB or 1.237995 TB usable. Even
the lowest `r=10`, five-minute, 6 Mbit/s sensitivity is 1.386 TB for video
alone, before request frames, exact model payloads, logs, analyses, or retry
attempts. The current disk therefore does not satisfy either safety margin.
The short scripted pilots are highly static and publication-invalid, so their
compression ratio is not a defensible substitute for production measurements.

## Current limitations

- Publication execution covers only T5/NM02/MuJoCo. The other profiles and
  scenarios have declarative/adaptor/preflight coverage but no publication
  engine path, so a full locked campaign would fail closed.
- Scripted, direct-scene MuJoCo, live-service, and disconnection/recovery
  evidence paths have clean audited pilots, including controlled failures.
  They are instrumentation-only. Production v4, v5, v6, and v7 are preserved
  `INVALID_HARNESS` attempts; there is no valid production pass/failure pair.
  The sole attempted production cell is T5/NM02/primary, under 0.5% of the
  minimum locked schedule, and produced no behavioral outcome.
- The post-v7 continuous-acquisition/CFR/cadence fix is unit-, integration-, and
  real-MuJoCo-liveness-tested but unpiloted. Service preflight attempt 9 gated
  only v7; attempt 10 freshly gates the proposed v8 pilot. The singular one-frame-per-call
  contract rejects a request containing multiple views, actual source
  throughput on this host is below 10 Hz and represented by explicit short
  holds, and exact raw HTTP upper/embedding evidence remains absent.
- A narrow, auditable Bernoulli-logit GLMM is implemented in
  `harness/mixed_effects.py` with explicit treatment coding, nested
  template/instance random intercepts, deterministic nested Gauss-Hermite
  marginal-likelihood integration with an independent quadrature-order check,
  fail-closed diagnostics, marginal contrasts, and deterministic mixed-model
  power simulation. This closes the code-scaffold gap only. It has not been
  regenerated on real excluded-pilot artifacts, and the exact factors,
  references, multiplicity-adjusted alpha, seed, sensitivity assumptions, and
  at least 1,000 simulations per candidate `r` remain unfrozen. The design's
  negative-binomial, positive-continuous, survival/censored, and human ordinal
  models are not implemented.
- Model backbone IDs/hashes and serving parameters must come from live
  preflight evidence. One primary Gemma model was observed in calibration, but
  the three immutable VLM backbones required by model sensitivity are not
  frozen or available as campaign provenance.
- The preregistration remains a draft, the locked repetition count is unset,
  and there is no frozen campaign ID, protocol hash, randomized schedule, or
  exact locked execution command. Exact approval cannot be requested yet.
- No real paired T5/B1 production pilot exists for an estimable GLMM or power
  selection; `r` remains unset. Available disk also fails the lowest `r=10`
  video sensitivity under either a 20% or 25% free-space reserve.
- Human and real-robot results are absent and must not be inferred from MuJoCo.
- Ethics/consent procedures and a release licence remain absent.
- One seed, one pilot, deterministic unit tests, or historical screenshots do
  not establish statistical reliability.
